To install: the installer opens with the desktop. If it does not:
    synapseos-installer

No desktop?  synapseos-plasma      starts Plasma and logs it
             synapseos-logs        collects everything into one file
             journalctl -b -p err  errors from this boot

No menu/window blur? Live blur needs OpenGL. In a VM the session falls
back to a pre-rendered frost wallpaper (desktop-frost.jpg). Force it with:
    synapseos-fix-blur
Desktop fails in a VM? Ctrl+Alt+F2, then:
    export QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software QSG_RHI_BACKEND=software
    unset KWIN_COMPOSE
    synapseos-plasma

Logs:  desktop    ~/.cache/synapseos/plasma-session.log
       installer  ~/.cache/calamares/session.log
